    "Notes Updated": "9/15/2025",
    "Scouting Notes": "Starter?\n Fastball has some good carry to it and should play well up in the zone, especially as it has some real armside run to it too. Hoping to see some more velo as he progresses. Sitting around 93 instead of touching it would go a long way.\n Curveball is a big breaker with pretty high spin\n Like the slider addition, bridges the gap between the fastball and curve better, but a definite WIP as a pitch itself\n Changeup shape isn't great, but I like it still. Takes 10 MPH off the fastball and kills spin well, think it can play as an above average pitch\n Command and control are both fine, but can improve for sure\n I like Carra, think there's real stuff here and solid feel. He's much better than his ACL surface stats would say.",
